# centralize_events_chat_alliance_3client_udp — client 1 (slot 0).
# Same shape as the unicast scenario but with an alliance handshake
# in front: c1 requests alliance with slot 2 (c3), c3 accepts on its
# side, then both exchange unicast chats. The chat path itself is
# unicast-only on the wire (no allies-only destination), so the
# alliance ceremony is what bakes the request/accept event variants
# into the baseline. c2 (passive witness) should see the alliance
# broadcast events but zero CTRL_CHAT events.
{"tick": 100, "op": "alliance_request", "from": 0, "to": 2}
{"tick": 300, "op": "chat", "dest": 2, "body": "hi ally c3 from c1"}
